    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. can u clarify the insurance part though? like, does the seller have to provide full coverage or just the bare minimum? i've heard different things about the level of protection required for high-value electronics.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Under CIF Incoterms 2020, the insurance requirement varies depending on the good's value. While the seller is obligated to procure minimum coverage that is normally considered adequate for the goods, they may extend this to commercial policies providing higher protection, if it aligns with standard business practices within the seller's sector. If the goods are of high value, as with electronics, the seller typically purchases more comprehensive coverage, with the insurance being in effect from the time of shipment to security presentation at the port of destination for final delivery. The buyer should be made aware of the insurance coverage upon contract completion.",
      "source": "target",
